AOT code caches linked into an image: load them in place (FEX 14c9268, on top of 0004)

WinPad's tools/cache2macho turns an AOT code cache (AOTCodeCacheWIP) into an
object file whose linker resolves every reference from the code to the data
area. On iOS that object is linked into the app, so the code arrives in the
app's signed text segment and FEX must neither copy nor write it.

CodeCache::LoadLinkedCache takes the image's three symbols: _meta (the cache
file without its code, behind a small "FXAM" header), _text (the code) and
_data (a zero-filled, writable data area). It fills the data area like
LoadCache does, but takes the code where the image put it: all pages count
as loaded, the code is ReadOnlyCode, and ExternalCode keeps the
MappedCodeCacheFile from unmapping it. LoadCache's header parsing, data area
fill and relocation grouping move into helpers shared by both.

On Linux the AOTImage option names a shared object made by
cache2macho --elf-asm. LoadCodeCache dlopens it and looks up
fexaot_<file id>_<config id>_{meta,text,data}; if the image has no code for
the binary, the cache file is used as before. This is how CI runs linked AOT
code; the iOS loader will look the same symbols up in the app itself.

